From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: arm_scmi: quiet expected fast-channel fallback noise

Two SCMI messages are emitted at dev_warn on every O6N (Radxa Orion) boot
even though nothing is wrong. They are benign, expected fallbacks, but at
warn level they dominate `dmesg -l err,warn` and read as errors.

1) driver.c, scmi_common_fastchannel_init() err_out path:

     arm-scmi ...: Failed to get FC for protocol X [MSG_ID:.. / RES_ID:..]
                   - ret:.. Using regular messaging.

   This fires once per (protocol, message, resource) that has no fast
   channel. When the platform is booted with `acpi_scmi_en=off` the SCMI
   fast-channel doorbell region is simply not described, so every
   perf/clock/etc. FC probe misses and the code correctly falls back to
   regular (mailbox) messaging -- the supported, functionally-equivalent
   transport. ~17 such lines appear on O6N. The success counterpart a few
   lines above already logs at dev_dbg ("Using valid FC for protocol..."),
   so the failure/fallback path is demoted to dev_dbg to match: the
   fallback itself is unchanged and still taken.

2) perf.c, scmi_perf_domain_init_fc()/attributes parse:

     arm-scmi ...: multiplier for domain N rounded

   Emitted when sustained_freq_khz*1000 is not an exact multiple of
   sustained_perf_level, so the integer mult_factor is rounded. This is an
   informational precision note, not an error -- the rounded multiplier is
   used deliberately. ~5 lines on O6N. Demoted to dev_dbg. The genuinely
   bad case just below (mult_factor == 0, "Wrong sustained perf/frequency")
   is left at dev_warn untouched.

Behaviour is identical; only the log level of these two benign expected
paths changes. arm_scmi is an upstream core driver -- the diff is kept to
the two dev_warn->dev_dbg tokens so it rebases across -rc bumps cleanly.

Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/driver.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/driver.c
@@ -2044,7 +2044,7 @@
 	ph->xops->xfer_put(ph, t);
 
 err_out:
-	dev_warn(ph->dev,
+	dev_dbg(ph->dev,
 		 "Failed to get FC for protocol %X [MSG_ID:%u / RES_ID:%u] - ret:%d. Using regular messaging.\n",
 		 pi->proto->id, message_id, domain, ret);
 }
--- a/drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/perf.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/perf.c
@@ -302,7 +302,7 @@
 					/ dom_info->sustained_perf_level;
 			if ((dom_info->sustained_freq_khz * 1000UL) %
 			    dom_info->sustained_perf_level)
-				dev_warn(ph->dev,
+				dev_dbg(ph->dev,
 					 "multiplier for domain %d rounded\n",
 					 dom_info->id);
 		}
